			<div class="content" id="post-content-1964007">
									

<p>I like this a <em>lot.</em> +1.</p>
<p>(Nitpick: Neither &quot;mesopause&quot; nor &quot;sugar maple tree&quot; are proper nouns. Fixed that for you.)</p>
<p>e: Oh, two other things.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-2033 is a sugar maple tree (<em>Acer saccharum</em>) measuring approximately 3m meters tall, with its trunk measuring approximately 0.2m in width.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>1. Foresters use a measure called &quot;diameter at breast height&quot;, or DBH, to describe tree-trunk sizes: it's the diameter at about 1.5 meters off the ground (chest height or thereabouts). Even if that's too jargony for your taste, though, I'd strongly recommend changing &quot;width&quot; to &quot;diameter&quot; &#8212; it's ambiguous as it is.</p>
<p>2. &quot;3m meters&quot;? For one thing, 3m is <em>extraordinarily</em> short for a sugar maple with a 20cm DBH. (I'd expect it to be 10m or so.) For another, you've effectively got &quot;meters&quot; in there twice.</p>

